  "id": "COMPOUND:32773 - PROTEIN:4923",
  "verbalization": "Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, (3beta)- is implicated in the interaction with Neuropilin-2 through a series of molecular pathways. The evidence suggests that this compound acts as a target for multiple downstream molecules, including Caragasinin B, Coniferin, and Radicinol, all of which are linked to Neuropilin-2. These intermediaries appear to be involved in signaling or functional processes that ultimately lead to the targeting of Neuropilin-2. The shared involvement of CD3 in two of the paths indicates a potential role in immune or cellular signaling, which may be a common mechanism across these pathways. The integration of these findings suggests that Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, (3beta)- may exert its effects through a network of targets that converge on Neuropilin-2, possibly through a shared or divergent pathway. The evidence supports a mechanism where the compound influences cellular processes that are ultimately directed toward Neuropilin-2, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
